Technical
### Changed

- Integrate the two divergent M9 Frontend Redesign branches into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes so the release can be tagged from a single point. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Re-introduce inline citation badges anchored in the sanitized Markdown answer via `AssistantMarkdown.Render(markdown, citations)`, which returns unanchored citations for the sources list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Make `SuggestedNextSteps` an `IReadOnlyList<SuggestedStep>` tagged with an action kind and optional target status, and render the first step as the primary action button in the ticket header. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a `CommandPalette` in `MainLayout`, opened with the `Ctrl/Cmd+K` chord, offering navigation entries built from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Apply status changes optimistically on the board and ticket detail view, rolling back to the prior state and showing a snackbar with the ProblemDetails `code` when the server rejects the transition. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace the `AssignTicketDialog` and `ChangeStatusDialog` modals with inline `MudMenu` popovers for changing status and assignee, and delete both dialog components. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Render assistant citations as inline `[n]` badges with a hover and focus tooltip, computed by the new `AnswerCitationLayout`, with a numbered sources list as fallback for unanchored citations. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Inject the active agent roster into the chat system prompt per request, loaded through `GetAgentsHandler`, so the model uses only valid agent names when assigning tickets. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Force `check_grounding` through `tool_choice` in `AgentLoop` once retrieval has produced passages and no check has run, so the grounding verdict is computed before the first streamed token. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Add `Theme/DesignTokens.cs` as the single source for palette, spacing, radius, elevation and semantic chip colours, rendered as `:root` custom properties and shared with `AppTheme`, and replace `KpiCard.Accent` strings with the `KpiAccent` enum. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Wrap the board card title link in a `board-card__title-row` div so Chrome no longer blockifies its `-webkit-box` and the two-line `-webkit-line-clamp` applies. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Fix the assistant composer panel by targeting `.assistant-chat` through `::deep`, so its padding and flex layout apply and the send button sits inside the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Give the `Category` column in the ticket queue a `140px` width and render its header with the uppercase `tickets-table__label` class so it no longer overlaps `Due`. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add a write-honesty and confirmation policy to the chat system prompt: never claim a change without a successful tool result, and do not re-ask when the user already requested the change. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert all timestamps in the ticket summary prompt built by `BuildTicketPrompt` to the `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` zone, so summaries match the local times shown in the UI. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Return `IsError: true` when `search_knowledge_base` hits a non-transient failure, distinct from the `unavailable` path, so the dashboard error rate reflects real failures. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Score grounding by meaning with the new `SemanticGroundingEvaluator`, which compares embeddings of answer sentences against retrieved passages, and keep `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` as the fallback. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))

